cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Coopetition-Gym: A Formally Grounded Benchmark for Mixed-Motive Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning under Strategic Coopetition"
type: software
version: "1.0.8"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >
  Coopetition-Gym is a benchmark platform for mixed-motive multi-agent reinforcement learning under
  strategic coopetition. The platform comprises twenty environments organized into four mechanism
  classes (interdependence and complementarity, trust and reputation dynamics, collective action and
  loyalty, sequential interaction and reciprocity); each environment carries a closed-form payoff
  structure and a calibrated interdependence matrix derived from a corresponding foundational technical
  report. Every environment exposes a parameterized reward layer configurable across three structurally
  distinct modes (private, integrated, cooperative); this separation of payoff from reward enables
  reward-type ablation as a first-class evaluation protocol. Four environments are calibrated against
  historically documented coopetitive relationships (Samsung-Sony LCD, Renault-Nissan Alliance, Apache
  HTTP Server, Apple iOS App Store). Their correspondence rubrics and unresolved score-version
  conflicts are documented separately; rubric percentages are not prediction accuracy. The
  platform exposes Gymnasium, PettingZoo Parallel, and PettingZoo AEC interfaces and ships 126
  reference algorithms.
authors:
  - given-names: Vik
    family-names: Pant
    affiliation: "Faculty of Information, University of Toronto"
  - given-names: Eric
    family-names: Yu
    affiliation: "Faculty of Information and Department of Computer Science, University of Toronto"
keywords:
  - multi-agent reinforcement learning
  - mixed-motive games
  - coopetition
  - benchmark
  - reward-type ablation
  - PettingZoo
  - Gymnasium

